{{-- A screenshot of the product.

     Real output: the components, the compiler and the grid that ship, captured
     from a running page. The rows behind it are a sample dataset and the
     caption says so, because a marketing image that implies somebody's real
     revenue is a different kind of claim.

     `shot`, `shotAlt` and `shotCaption` come from the page's own server script.
     Partials are included into the page's scope, so they are read directly:
     passing them as props would arrive empty, since stx drops props between
     components in this version. --}}
<figure class="mt-12">
  <div class="overflow-hidden bg-panel border border-line rounded-xl">
    <img
      src="{{ shot }}"
      alt="{{ shotAlt }}"
      width="1240"
      height="600"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="block h-auto w-full"
    >
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-subtle text-xs">{{ shotCaption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
